WEB SOURCE: web/src/components/forms/Combobox.tsx  (WAI-ARIA 1.2 editable combobox / autocomplete)
TESTS: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/ComboboxTests.cs (53 headless tests)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Composition: the web source builds its OWN editable input + <ul role="listbox"> (it does NOT wrap a
  native <select>), so the native surface mirrors that with a tokenized input Border hosting a borderless
  TextBox + a trailing cluster (an in-flight ProgressRing, a clear (x) TsButton, a chevron-toggle TsButton)
  and the option listbox in a Popup anchored under the input. NOT the platform ComboBox; NOT the existing
  Components/Forms TsCombobox primitive (that wraps AutoSuggestBox) - this is the higher-level shared surface.
- Data sources (web hooks -> native seams, P1/S8): useTranslation -> ILocalizer (P1/S10);
  useAnnouncer -> IAnnouncerBus (the shared AnnouncerBus, web announce()); useId -> WinUI automation peer.
  The web `options` union (static array | async loader (query, AbortSignal)) -> IComboboxOptionsSource with
  StaticComboboxOptionsSource (filters via the shared, unit-tested Core ComboboxFilter == web defaultFilter)
  and AsyncComboboxOptionsSource (ComboboxOptionLoader + CancellationToken == the web AbortSignal). The option
  type reuses the shared Core record TeslaSync.App.Core.Forms.ComboOption (DRY; not re-declared).
- Shared components used (web @/components/a11y) -> native Components/A11y TsVisuallyHidden (hidden label) +
  the shared announcer bus; trailing affordances are shared Components/UI TsButton (Icon variant).
- States reproduced (every branch the web source actually renders):
    * loading  -> in-flight ProgressRing + a "Loading" listbox row (web loadingProp || asyncLoading; L640).
    * empty    -> "No results" row (web visibleOptions.length === 0 && !loading; L630). The async loader's
                  error path collapses here exactly as the web .catch resolves to [] (L255-260) - mapped in
                  AsyncComboboxOptionsSource; a cancelled (superseded) keystroke is dropped, not shown.
    * results  -> option rows with a keyboard active descendant (wrap-around Up/Down, Home/End; web L398-466).
    * overflow -> "{{count}} more - refine search" row when filtered > maxVisibleOptions (web L675-686).
  The web Combobox is a CONTROLLED presentational primitive with no query-freshness or connectivity concept,
  so it has NO stale/offline chrome - and none is invented (honesty covenant: no drift in either direction).
- Behaviour parity: type-ahead opens + filters/debounces; Enter commits the active option (or, in
  allowFreeText, the trimmed text -> onFreeTextCommit + onChange(null)); Esc closes and reverts the text to
  the selected label; Tab commits the highlighted option then continues tab order; the clear button resets
  selection+text and reopens; async fetch is debounced (default 200ms) and cancels the previous request on
  each keystroke (web AbortController). Disabled options are never committed (consistent with the shared
  Core combobox model + its existing ComboboxModelTests).
- i18n (web t() keys -> P1/S10, all 8 already in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw, verified 8/8 each):
    combobox.noResults "No results" | resultsCountOne "1 result" | resultsCount "{{count}} results" |
    loading "Loading" | clearAria "Clear selection" | closeListAria "Hide options" |
    openListAria "Show options" | moreHidden "{{count}} more - refine search" (em dash preserved).
  Catalog values use the native {0} token; web fallbacks use i18next {{count}} - both are interpolated
  (ComboboxRegistration.Interpolate), matching the shipped BulkActionsToolbar pattern. No English literals
  in native code; every visible string flows through the localizer.
- Accessibility: the input carries the ComboBox control type + an IExpandCollapseProvider automation peer
  (web aria-expanded), the accessible name (web label / aria-label, optionally TsVisuallyHidden), and every
  interactive control (input, clear, chevron, each option row) has an accessible name. Result-count changes
  are announced politely through the shared announcer (web announce()); WinUI scales with the system font.
- Diagnostics (P1/S11): emits `view.opened slug=Combobox` once on Loaded. PII-safe (slug only; never the
  query text, option labels, or committed value).

